{"abstract":[{"text":"The complement of a graph, as a lazy view. Made by ","type":"text"},{"code":"complementView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ComplementView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices and their indices are the base’s. Row ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists every index ","type":"text"},{"code":"j ≠ i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"base’s row ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lacks, in ascending order. Producing a row costs O(deg + n\/64 + output) and one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocation. The complement of a sparse graph has Θ(n²) edges, so a full traversal is Θ(n²).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An edge’s position is its cell of the adjacency matrix, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Cell(source: i, target: j)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ordered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row-major as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s positions are. An undirected edge has ","type":"text"},{"code":"source < target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". There","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are no edge indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphAdaptor"},{"type":"text","text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"maps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[map, of:]"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). Its edges are not the base’s, so edge maps don’t read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/Cell","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/CellRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/UndirectedEdges"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/base"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/source(checkedEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/target(checkedEdgeAt:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/Gr